      "Confirm by hand: POST the same deep query yourself and see `\"data\"` come back with a fully-resolved 8-level-deep `ofType` chain -- proof the server will walk however deep you ask it to.",
      "GET /flag once you've sent a query with an `ofType` chain at least as deep as the probe's (8 hops) and gotten `\"data\"` back for it.",
      "Real fix: add a query-depth-limit validation rule (reject the query document before execution once nesting exceeds a small fixed maximum, e.g. 5-10) rather than trusting resolvers to bound themselves."
